-- EXPECT-ERROR: performs IO but declares no grant
mod Main do
  -- R1 stage D reject witness (2026-08-10) — the end of ambient IO.
  --
  -- Stages A–C made a DECLARED grant enforceable, and left the default
  -- ambient: a `main` with no capability parameter performed IO freely. That
  -- adoption contract is what let the grant check ship without breaking a
  -- single program, and it is also what kept the honest claim down to "a
  -- program that STATES its grant cannot exceed it".
  --
  -- Here every `needs` line is truthful and every earlier check passes. The
  -- program is rejected because it never says what authority it runs under.
  -- Accept companion t171 adds exactly that, and nothing else.
  needs IO.Console
  needs IO.FileWrite

  fn main() : () do
    match file_write("/tmp/t171_out", "d") do
      Ok(_)  -> println("ok")
      Err(_) -> println("e")
    end
  end
end
